\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 13.6622H7.77047\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</span> Notes</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5850-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-5850-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"5850\" data-servings=\"8\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Main Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">8-ounce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">wheel of Brie cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">The star of the dish</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">sheet</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">puff pastry</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Thawed for easy wrapping</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fruit preserves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Apricot or raspberry work beautifully</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">egg</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">beaten egg</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For a glossy finish</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">water</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To mix with the egg</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Optional Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">chopped nuts</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Walnuts or pecans for added crunch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">honey</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For drizzling on top</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-5850-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5850\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking sheet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Lined with parchment paper</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Rolling Pin&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For rolling out puff pastry</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5850-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-5850-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5850\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">On a lightly floured surface, roll out the puff pastry sheet to smooth out any seams.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place the Brie wheel in the center of the pastry.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Spoon the fruit preserves on top of the Brie.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Sprinkle optional nuts over the preserves, if using.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Fold the pastry edges up over the top of the Brie, pleating as needed to seal.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Brush the pastry all over with the beaten egg mixed with water.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place the wrapped Brie on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-8\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bake for 20–25 minutes, or until the pastry is golden brown.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-9\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Let rest for 5 minutes, then drizzle with honey if desired.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5850-step-0-10\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Slice and serve warm with crackers or sliced baguette.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-5850-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>6g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients for a delicious Baked Brie experience!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Baked-Brie-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for Baked Brie including Brie cheese, puff pastry, fruit preserves, and optional nuts and honey on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-5848\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Baked-Brie-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Baked-Brie-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 (8-ounce) wheel of Brie cheese</strong> – the star of the dish</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 sheet of puff pastry</strong> – thawed for easy wrapping</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons fruit preserves</strong> – apricot or raspberry work beautifully</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 egg</strong> – beaten, for a glossy finish</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon water</strong> – to mix with the egg</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Optional: chopped nuts</strong> – walnuts or pecans for added crunch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Optional: honey</strong> – for drizzling on top</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-baked-brie\"><strong>How to Make Baked Brie</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to impress your guests with this delightful Baked <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brie\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brie</a>! With a preparation time of about 15 minutes and a cooking time of 20-25 minutes, you&#8217;ll have a warm, gooey treat ready in no time. Don&#8217;t forget to let it rest for 5 minutes before serving!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Step-by-Step-Baked-Brie-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of Baked Brie, including preheating the oven, rolling out puff pastry, placing Brie with fruit preserves, and wrapping it for baking.\" class=\"wp-image-5849\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Step-by-Step-Baked-Brie-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Step-by-Step-Baked-Brie-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Roll Out the Pastry</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On a lightly floured surface, roll out the puff pastry sheet to smooth out any seams.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Place the Brie</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the Brie wheel in the center of the pastry.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add Fruit Preserves</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Spoon the fruit preserves on top of the Brie.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Sprinkle Nuts (Optional)</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sprinkle optional nuts over the preserves, if using.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Fold the Pastry</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fold the pastry edges up over the top of the Brie, pleating as needed to seal.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Brush with Egg Wash</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Brush the pastry all over with the beaten egg mixed with water.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Prepare for Baking</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the wrapped Brie on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Bake</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake for 20–25 minutes, or until the pastry is golden brown.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 10: Let it Rest</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let rest for 5 minutes, then drizzle with honey if desired.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 11: Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Slice and serve warm with crackers or sliced baguette.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Appetizer</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>French</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>5 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>45 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with crackers or sliced baguette</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-baked-brie\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Baked Brie</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose a high-quality Brie for the best flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the cheese sit at room temperature for 30 minutes before baking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with honey or fig jam for a delightful sweetness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in puff pastry for a flaky, golden crust.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with an assortment of crackers and fresh fruit for variety.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-baked-brie\"><strong>How to Serve this Baked Brie</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with crispy baguette slices for a delightful crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with fresh fruit like apples, pears, or grapes for a sweet contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with honey or maple syrup for a touch of sweetness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a sprinkle of nuts, like walnuts or pecans, for extra texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include a side of fig or apricot jam for a fruity kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer a selection of crackers for a variety of flavors and textures.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with herbs like rosemary or thyme for a fresh aroma.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a colorful veggie platter for a healthy option.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your Baked Brie later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Baked Brie Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow Baked Brie to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap it tightly in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in an airtight container in the fridge.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consume within 3-4 days for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Baked Brie</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap cooled Baked Brie in plastic wrap, then foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in a freezer-safe container or bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thaw in the fridge before reheating.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Baked Brie</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove wrapping and place on a baking sheet.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat for about 10-15 minutes until warm and gooey.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with your favorite crackers or fruit!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Do you take the rind off brie when you bake it?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>No, you do not need to remove the rind from brie before baking it. The rind is edible and adds a lovely texture and flavor to the dish. When baked, the rind helps to contain the creamy cheese inside, making for a delightful experience as you dip into the warm, gooey center.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What temperature should brie be baked at?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Brie is best baked at 350°F (175°C). This temperature allows the cheese to melt evenly without burning the outside. It’s the perfect heat to achieve that gooey, melty goodness that everyone loves about baked brie.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How long to cook brie in the oven at 400 degrees?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>If you choose to bake brie at 400°F (200°C), it typically takes about 10-15 minutes. Keep an eye on it to ensure it doesn’t overcook; you want it to be warm and gooey, not bubbling over. A good indicator is when the cheese starts to soften and the rind turns a lovely golden color.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Do you put jam on brie before baking?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, adding jam or a fruit preserve on top of the brie before baking is a fantastic idea! It enhances the flavor and adds a sweet contrast to the creamy cheese. Popular choices include fig jam, apricot preserves, or even a homemade berry compote. Just spread a thin layer on top before wrapping it in pastry or placing it in a baking dish.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There you have it—your guide to making the most delightful Baked Brie! This dish is not just simple; it’s a warm hug for your taste buds. So gather your friends, share some laughs, and enjoy this gooey, cheesy goodness. You’ll be amazed at how something so easy can bring so much joy. Happy baking!</p>\n",
